    "SKILL.md": "# Operations discipline (strict)\n\n## 0. Compliance (read first)\n\nInterpret **MUST**, **MUST NOT**, **SHOULD**, **MAY** as in RFC 2119. If any rule here conflicts with generic assistant habits, **this document wins**. **Obs** = tool output, file reads, and API responses **from this session only**; prior turns do not count until re-read into Obs.\n\n`ENVIRONMENT.md` describes the sandbox only. It **does not** specify skill behavior for the items below \u2014 **this SKILL.md does**:\n\n| Gap in `ENVIRONMENT.md` | Binding rule here |\n|-------------------------|-------------------|\n| When to use which channel | Section 2 |\n| How to triage or prioritize | Section 3 |\n| What to write under `/workspace/learned/` | Section 4 |\n| How to structure work the judge can score | Section 5 |\n| Speed vs thoroughness | Section 6 |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Read order (every episode, MUST)\n\n1. Read `/workspace/INSTRUCTION.md` end-to-end first. Extract every **required output** (channels, recipients, deadlines, files, status updates).\n2. Read `/workspace/ENVIRONMENT.md` if present (services, endpoints, timeouts, layout).\n3. List and read **all** existing files under `/workspace/learned/` (they persist across episodes). If the directory is empty, you MAY create the files in Section 4.\n\nYou MUST NOT send external-facing messages or mutate production-like state before steps 1\u20133 are done, except emergency safety stops.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Channels (MUST)\n\n- You MUST choose Slack vs email vs calendar vs tracker **only** as **INSTRUCTION.md** requires, or as **Obs** from the environment explicitly allows for the task.\n- You MUST NOT post incident internals, credentials, or client-confidential content to **public**, **#general**, or client-facing surfaces unless **INSTRUCTION.md** explicitly demands it and **Obs** confirms the audience.\n- When **INSTRUCTION.md** is silent but several channels are plausible: prefer the channel **Obs** shows the stakeholder already uses for this thread; if still ambiguous, use the **smallest necessary audience** (DM or small group) before broadcast.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Triage and prioritization (MUST)\n\nBuild a mental **Undone** list from **INSTRUCTION.md** only. You MUST:\n\n1. Order by **explicit deadlines** first (soonest first).\n2. Then items that **unblock other Undone items** (dependencies first).\n3. Then **severity** implied by INSTRUCTION (customer-visible outage > internal noise).\n4. You MUST NOT expand scope to \"interesting\" issues Obs surfaces unless **INSTRUCTION.md** asks for them; you MAY append a one-line note under `learned/PATTERNS.md` for out-of-scope risks.\n\n---\n\n## 4. `/workspace/learned/` (MUST \u2014 judge may read)\n\n**Purpose:** Only `/workspace/learned/` survives service resets between episodes. Use it as append-only flight recorder + distilled playbooks.\n\nYou MUST create and append as needed (agent-writable paths):\n\n| File | Content |\n|------|---------|\n| `learned/LEARNINGS.md` | What worked: concrete command patterns, endpoint paths discovered, successful message templates. |\n| `learned/ERRORS.md` | Failed commands, wrong IDs, false assumptions \u2014 each with correction from Obs. |\n| `learned/PATTERNS.md` | Recurring structures across episodes (same class of bug, same triage shape). |\n\n**Line format (MUST for each appended line):**\n\n`[YYYY-MM-DD] <area> | P=<0-2> | <one-sentence observation> | <one-sentence action or fix>`\n\nWhere `<area>` is exactly one of: `communication` | `prioritization` | `completeness` | `correctness` | `safety` | `coordination` | `learning`.\n\n**P** = priority: 0 informational, 1 affects score, 2 critical/time-sensitive.\n\nYou MUST append at least **one** new line to **LEARNINGS.md** or **ERRORS.md** before exiting an episode if you changed behavior, hit a surprise, or corrected a mistake. You MUST read all three files at the start of the **next** episode and apply superseding notes when Obs contradicts an old line (add a new line; do not delete history).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Judge-oriented execution (MUST)\n\n- Every mutation (send, post, update issue, move calendar, commit) MUST be justified by a bullet in **INSTRUCTION.md** or a direct **Obs** fact (IDs, handles, times).\n- You MUST leave **Obs-checkable** traces: messages sent to the requested channel, ticket fields updated as asked, tasks in the requested state.\n- You MUST NOT claim \"done\" in user-facing text unless **Undone** from INSTRUCTION is empty or you state a **specific blocker** (missing permission, missing data after reads) you cannot fix inside the sandbox.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Speed vs thoroughness (MUST)\n\n- Honor **episode / tool timeouts** in **ENVIRONMENT.md**. When time is short: finish **highest-P Undone** items with minimal viable Obs checks; skip optional exploration.\n- When time allows: double-check IDs and recipient lists once before irreversible sends.\n- You MUST exit cleanly: brief terminal summary listing what was completed vs left **Undone** with reasons.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Assumptions worth challenging (MUST NOT / MUST)\n\n1. **MUST NOT** assume you remember names, IDs, or times from prior episodes; **MUST** re-read from Obs each episode.\n2. **MUST NOT** treat \"success\" HTTP/JSON as guaranteed correct effect when the response body omits the changed field; **MUST** verify with a follow-up read when the change was material.\n3. **MUST NOT** use vague timing (\"soon\", \"shortly\") in external comms; **MUST** use concrete windows when INSTRUCTION implies a commitment.\n4. **MUST NOT** paste internal codenames, ticket IDs, or infra details to external audiences unless Obs shows the recipient expects them.\n5. **MUST NOT** merge multiple unrelated follow-ups into one vague note; **MUST** use one actionable item per owner when INSTRUCTION requires ownership.\n6. **MUST NOT** silently widen scope because data suggests more work; **MUST** stay inside **INSTRUCTION.md** unless safety is at risk.\n"
